---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../../styles/afterframe-a.css';

/* Arm "a" of the /afterframe test (see src/lib/afterframe.ts). Converted
   from the standalone concept contact-sheet-3.html; the direction contract is the first
   comment inside the page root (Astro strips a slot's leading comment; a
   deeper one survives). */
---
<Base title="Afterframe · Keep what stayed with you" description="A new kind of film companion for Plex. Reach back to a moment playing on your Apple TV, keep the frame and its words without interrupting the film, then share it beautifully." fonts={['family=Schibsted+Grotesk:ital,wght@0,400..900;1,400..900', 'family=Courier+Prime:ital,wght@0,400;0,700;1,400', 'family=Newsreader:ital,opsz,wght@0,6..72,300..800;1,6..72,300..800']}>

<div class="af-root">
<!--
DIRECTION CONTRACT · seed 8534e8c8 · mode persuade
THESIS: A moment kept is a frame circled in grease pencil on a proof sheet; the page IS the sheet, and the pencil is the visitor's cursor. Third cut: the frame's journey into a real group chat is shown, the header line corrects Keep to Share in pencil while the sharing sections are in view, and the never-stops section holds the loop. Second cut: every frame is a real capture from the owner's library, the sheet re-strings by hour or by title, and the library is an archive box of sleeved sheets. Refuses the floating-phone dark hero.
OWN-WORLD: glossy silver-gelatin black sheet on a matte bench, film-base strips with printed perforations and white edge lettering, one china-marker orange for every mark, paper-white 8x10 prints, Schibsted Grotesk display, Courier Prime typed labels, Newsreader italic notes. State is a mark (circle, cross, check), never a hue.
STORY: visitor reads one line, sees a frame circled out of a running strip, understands "keep it without stopping the film", joins the early list.
FIRST VIEWPORT: headline top-left across two columns; below, left 60% a three-strip proof sheet with frame 14 (01:11:40) circled and its edge label lit, right 40% the circled frame as an 8x10 print with typed title/timecode and an italic note, then the two CTAs.
FORM: proof sheet, candidate 3 of 7 (assigned). Raises: frame pitch snaps to the 10s index (cutting bench); solid mark for the committed frame, faint for the rest (pattern envelope); crowded index strip against one bare print (obi band).
FINISH: unreviewed and undocumented is unfinished; this build ends with the finish review, the verdict, and DESIGN.md
-->
<svg width="0" height="0" style="position:absolute" aria-hidden="true"><filter id="grease" x="-10%" y="-10%" width="120%" height="120%"><feTurbulence type="fractalNoise" baseFrequency=".9" numOctaves="2" seed="3" result="n"/><feDisplacementMap in="SourceGraphic" in2="n" scale="2.2" xChannelSelector="R" yChannelSelector="G"/></filter></svg>
<header class="top">
  <div class="wrap">
    <a class="brand" href="#main" aria-label="Afterframe home"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/shots/afterframe/icon.png" alt="" width="28" height="28"><span>Afterframe</span></a>
    <nav aria-label="Sections">
      <a href="#how">How it works</a>
      <a href="#library">Your library</a>
      <a href="#sharing">Sharing</a>
      <a href="#faq">FAQ</a>
    </nav>
    <a class="btn btn-grease" href="/afterframe/a/go/">Join the early list</a>
  </div>
  <div class="runner"><div class="wrap"><span class="type"><span class="swap"><span class="keep">Keep</span><span class="share" aria-hidden="true">Share</span><svg class="strike" viewBox="0 0 100 20" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true"><path pathLength="1" d="M2 12 C 30 9, 60 13, 98 8"/></svg></span> what stayed with you</span><span class="type right" id="runner-right">Proof sheet · 22 Sep 2026</span></div></div>
</header>

