          <figcaption>Now · the film never stops</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── How it works ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="steps wrap" id="how" aria-labelledby="h-how">
  <div class="sec-head">
    <h2 id="h-how">Notice. Reach back. Keep&nbsp;it.</h2>
    <p class="measure">Five frames, in the order they happen. Capture now. Write later. Or never write at all.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="sheet">
    <div class="strips">
      <div class="strip-title"><span><b>How it works</b> · five frames in order</span><span>Now · Choose Moment · the plate · a note · Export</span></div>
      <div class="strip" style="--n:5">
        <div class="edge t"><span>1 · notice</span><span>2 · reach back</span><span>3 · keep</span><span>4 · yours</span><span>5 · share</span></div>
        <div class="frame"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="920" height="497" src="/shots/afterframe/stills/s2-notice.jpg" alt="In the Mood for Love playing, seen in Afterframe's Now screen"></div>
        <div class="frame"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="920" height="497" src="/shots/afterframe/stills/s2-reach.jpg" alt="Choose Moment: drag to hold a moment across the indexed timeline"></div>
        <div class="frame"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="840" height="454" src="/shots/afterframe/stills/s2-keep.jpg" alt="The orange capture plate"></div>
        <div class="frame"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="840" height="454" src="/shots/afterframe/stills/s2-yours.jpg" alt="Add a note: What made you stop here?"></div>
        <div class="frame"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="840" height="454" src="/shots/afterframe/stills/step-share.jpg" alt="Export: Save to Photos, Save, Share"></div>
        <div class="edge b"><span>Now</span><span>Choose Moment</span><span>Now</span><span>Note</span><span>Export</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="captions">
        <div><h3>Notice something</h3><p>Keep watching. Afterframe observes the active Plex session, on Apple TV or any Plex client, without taking control of it.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Reach back</h3><p>Drag to hold a moment across the recent indexed timeline, or jump across the full runtime.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Keep it</h3><p>Afterframe secures the frame and its place in the film, then quietly works toward a higher-quality image when one is available.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Make it yours</h3><p>Keep the moment as it is, preserve available dialogue, or answer one question:</p><p class="q">What made you stop here?</p></div>
        <div><h3>Share it</h3><p>Send a clean image to a friend, or include dialogue and timecode when the context matters. The private original stays in Afterframe.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── Library ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="library" id="library" aria-labelledby="h-lib">
  <div class="wrap pair">
    <div>
      <h2 id="h-lib">Your taste, told in&nbsp;moments.</h2>
      <p class="measure" style="margin-top:18px">Afterframe is not another list of what you watched. It is a history of what you noticed.</p>
      <p class="measure" style="margin-top:14px">Your captures gather in Weave, a visual library where written moments have room to breathe and unannotated frames remain complete. Switch to Ribbon to see the shape of your attention across a film or episode: where moments clustered, where one image stood alone, and which scenes asked you to write something down.</p>
      <ul class="claims">
        <li>Film or episode identity</li>
        <li>Meaningful timecode</li>
        <li>Optional captured dialogue</li>
        <li>Optional personal note</li>
        <li>Search by title, line, note, or time</li>
        <li>Tonight: everything you kept this evening</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="phone-row">
      <figure>
        <div class="phone"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="920" height="2000" src="/shots/afterframe/shots/library-invite.webp" alt="Weave view: 133 captures, a grid of frames from The Invite with timecodes and Note buttons"></div>
        <figcaption>Weave · 133 captures</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <div class="phone"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="920" height="2000" src="/shots/afterframe/ribbon.webp" alt="Ribbon view: The Paper, S02E03, nine captures laid along a 24:40 timeline"></div>
        <figcaption>Ribbon · one episode, nine moments</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="box" aria-label="The archive box: one sheet per title">
